    "faq_bino": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_row_1": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What does 10x50 mean?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The first number is magnification: 10X makes distant objects appear 10 times closer. The second is the objective lens diameter, 50 mm. Larger lenses let in more light.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_2": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are the Polar HD binoculars waterproof?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The Polar HD is rainproof rather than fully waterproof. Its nitrogen-purged construction protects the internal optics from moisture, so it is built for rain, mist and humid conditions. We don't recommend submerging it.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the field of view?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The field of view is 6.8°, which is 360 ft wide at 1000 yards. A wider field of view makes it easier to find and follow your subject.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_4": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How close can I focus?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The close focus distance is 26.2 ft.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_5": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the eye relief?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The eye relief is 12 mm. Eye relief is how far your eye can sit from the eyepiece and still see the full image; more is generally more comfortable, especially for people who wear glasses.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will they fit my eyes?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The interpupillary distance (the spacing between the two barrels) adjusts from 56–72 mm, which suits most adults.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_7": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How big and heavy are they?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>They measure 6.65 × 7.7 in (height × width) and weigh 29 oz. The 50mm objective lenses gather more light than the smaller models in the line.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_8": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What are they best for?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The Polar HD is a good fit for bird watching, wildlife viewing, hunting, hiking and sporting events.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_9": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I use them on a tripod?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. They are tripod adaptable, using a standard tripod adapter (sold separately), for steady, hands-free viewing during long observation sessions.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_row_10": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is your warranty and return policy?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>[Warranty and returns details to be added.]</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
